*> The guardian beam (docs/protocol/34-entity-models-6-overworld-hostiles-arthropods-slimes.md 11.4 and 11.6): a guardian with an active attack target (entry 17, EN-TGT: an entity of the replica or
*> the local player) draws the beam from its eye to the middle of the target, as two crossing planes that turn with the attack time (strips cut where the scrolling texture repeats, the atlas
*> holding one image per slot) and the sparkle cap, each quad from both sides, tinted by the attack scale. Expected vertices from an independent script (scratchpad/models/guardian_beam.py,
*> written from the document text) for a guardian at (10.5, 64, 10.5), a target 1.4 high at (14.5, 64, 10.5), attack time 30 ticks (partial tick 1), eye at (10, 64, 10).
